  "limitations": [
    "baml-py 0.226.3 starts an internal span per expression-function call but never finalizes or exports it (drain_stats: finalized=sent=0 even after flush), so no runtime-internal trace payload is exported.",
    "BAML_TRACE_FILE and BAML_TRACER have no observable effect on expression functions in the 0.226.3 Python runtime; no OTLP exporter is embedded and the Boundary cloud publisher stays inactive without an API key (no network egress; benchmark fixture data only).",
    "Collector FunctionLogs record BAML function names (e.g. ImputerFit, LogRegFit), not custom OTel pipeline.stage.<step>.<op> span names; with_options(tags=...) is not retained on expression-function logs and tracing.trace cannot wrap BAML calls (Call ID mismatch).",
    "Monolithic pipeline functions emit a single FunctionLog, so this runner executes each stage from Python for per-stage observability at the cost of extra Python<->BAML bridge crossings.",
    "FunctionLog.timing.duration_ms is None for expression functions: runtime_only_s is null and bridge overhead is approximated by the bridge_probe operation."
  ],
